LeetCode solutikn - Swap Nodes in Pairs

Approach: Iterative Linked List

Problem
Swap every two adjacent nodes in a linked list and return the modified list.

Example
Input: "1 → 2 → 3 → 4"
Output: "2 → 1 → 4 → 3"

solution

class Solution {
    public ListNode swapPairs(ListNode head) {

        ListNode dummy = new ListNode(0);
        dummy.next = head;

        ListNode prev = dummy;

        while (prev.next != null && prev.next.next != null) {

            ListNode first = prev.next;
            ListNode second = first.next;

            first.next = second.next;
            second.next = first;
            prev.next = second;

            prev = first;
        }

        return dummy.next;
    }
}


Approach
1. Create a dummy node before the head.
2. Use "prev" to track the node before the current pair.
3. Use "first" and "second" to identify the two nodes.
4. Change their "next" references to swap them.
5. Move "prev" forward and repeat until fewer than two nodes remain.

Complexity Analysis

- Time Complexity: O(n) – Each node is processed once.
- Space Complexity: O(1) – Only a few extra pointers are used.

Key Learning

Learned how to swap adjacent nodes in a linked list by changing references without changing the node values.
